# BLAKE2b pooled jobs: never hand a miner an unsplit coinbase
#
# Upstream-facing version of lazarus/patches/datum-gateway-split-only.patch, with the
# Lazarus-specific user-agent bump removed so it can be proposed as-is.
#
# Target: FlyTheElephant1/datum_gateway master @ 121edd06 (== test/console-collapse-pr14-pr17)
# Verified: applies with no fuzz, and `cmake --build` is clean with no new warnings.
#
#   git clone https://github.com/FlyTheElephant1/datum_gateway.git
#   cd datum_gateway && patch -p1 < datum-gateway-blake2b-split-upstream.patch
#
# The bug: in send_mining_notify, `if (new_block) cbselect = 0;` runs before the BLAKE2b
# branch, and the subsidy-only pairing below it is gated on !stratum_job_is_blake2b(j). So a
# SHA256d miner gets a genuinely empty job on a new block, but a BLAKE2b miner gets coinbase
# type 0 -- which carries no coinbaser outputs -- attached to the *full* template, fees and
# all. A block found on that job pays the pool script alone and the DATUM split is lost. The
# miner keeps that job until the next work update, so the exposure is the whole gap, not an
# instant.
#
